## 11. Common Placement Interview Questions

**Q1. What is CPU scheduling?**  
It selects a process from the ready queue to execute on the CPU.

**Q2. What is the difference between SJF and SRTF?**  
SJF is non-preemptive, while SRTF is preemptive and considers remaining burst time.

**Q3. Which algorithm can cause the convoy effect?**  
FCFS.

**Q4. Which algorithm can cause starvation?**  
SJF and Priority Scheduling can cause starvation.

**Q5. How can starvation be reduced?**  
By using aging.

**Q6. What happens when the Round Robin time quantum is very large?**  
Round Robin behaves more like FCFS.

**Q7. What is response time?**  
The time from a process's arrival until it first gets the CPU.

**Q8. What is the difference between waiting time and turnaround time?**  
Turnaround time is total time spent in the system after arrival; waiting time is time spent waiting in the ready queue.

**Q9. Which scheduling algorithm gives the minimum average waiting time?**  
SJF is optimal under the standard assumptions when burst times are known; its preemptive counterpart is SRTF.

**Q10. Why is context switching an overhead?**  
The OS must save and restore execution state, which takes time that does not directly advance the process's work.

